+// AO2DC diagnostics: raw float rings of (a) every frame the game submits, captured in SubmitFrame
+// before non-finite samples are replaced and before any host processing (premix), and (b) every
+// buffer handed to SDL, including underrun silence (post-host). Writers only memcpy into
+// preallocated slots guarded by per-slot sequence numbers; readers (the game-module filter
+// recorder's worker thread) copy a time window out. No allocation, file I/O or formatting on the
+// audio paths. Timestamps are steady_clock nanoseconds, shared with the game module.
